Associating a Webex Bot to a Cisco Workflows Webhook

Bot Access Token: ... Used in HTTP Requests towards Webex

Webhook API Key: ... Generated by Workflows when Webhook was created

Encoded API Key: ... Encoding the API Key avoids problems when using with URLs

Webhook URL: ... Generated by Workflows when Webhook was created. Contains the API Key

Encoded Webhook URL: Replacing the API Key with the Encoded API Key above


Associate a Bot to a Cisco Workflows Webhook

```
curl -X POST "https://webexapis.com/v1/webhooks" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <BOT_ACCESS_TOKEN>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "My Webex Bot Message Created Webhook",
    "targetUrl": "https://us.workflows.meraki.com/webhooks/02QFBRDWXDLO92Ng8NoCvbhsiNdsAlKYk9S?api_key=<URL_ENCODED_MERAKI_KEY>",
    "resource": "messages",
    "event": "created",
    "filter": "mentionedPeople=me"
  }'
```

id: ... Returned from Curl command identifying the Association

List all Webex Bot Associations

```sh
curl -X GET "https://webexapis.com/v1/webhooks" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <BOT_ACCESS_TOKEN>" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json"
```

Delete an Association

```sh
curl -X DELETE "https://webexapis.com/v1/webhooks/<ID_RETURNED_FROM_ASSOCIATION>" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <BOT_ACCESS_TOKEN>"
```
